tandem (3.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Two formats Linux uses itself now open with a double click: .AppImage and
    .jar. The reason is the same one that started this project - the owner
    downloaded something, clicked it, and nothing happened - and for these two
    the cause is not Wine, it is Linux.
  * An AppImage arrives from the browser without the execute bit, and a file
    without that bit is not offered to the system as a program at all. The
    click opens an archive manager, or does nothing, and the file gets blamed.
    Tandem sets the bit: the owner double-clicked, he has already said he wants
    to run it, and asking permission for the one thing that makes that possible
    would be theatre.
  * appimageinfo.py reads the header without executing anything. The AppImage
    generation and the processor it was built for live in the first twenty
    bytes, and the payload's own header says how many bytes it should have - so
    an interrupted download, which is the most common way an AppImage fails for
    a lay user, is diagnosed as an interrupted download instead of as a broken
    program. The payload offset it computes was checked against the runtime's
    own --appimage-offset on a real AppImage: same number, with nothing run.
  * FUSE is worked around instead of demanded. Ubuntu dropped libfuse2 from the
    default install in 22.04 and every second-generation AppImage mounts itself
    with it, so a fresh download on a current Zorin fails with a dlopen message
    and nothing else. Tandem recognises that failure and retries with
    --appimage-extract-and-run, which needs nothing installed; it says so
    afterwards, and only after the program actually worked. Measured with
    /dev/fuse removed: exit code 127, and the workaround opened the program.
  * The AppImage goes into the applications menu, using the desktop entry the
    AppImage itself carries. This is the same problem "tandem programas" exists
    for - on Wayland GNOME does not re-read the application list - except here
    it has a real fix. Extraction does not mount anything, so it works on
    exactly the machines that have no FUSE; that was verified, not assumed.
    An entry whose file has since been deleted removes itself.
  * jarinfo.py answers the two questions Java answers in words nobody outside
    the trade can act on. "no main manifest attribute" becomes "this file is a
    piece of a program, not a program" - the two kinds of .jar are
    indistinguishable from the outside, and the owner has no way of knowing he
    downloaded the wrong one. "UnsupportedClassVersionError: class file version
    65.0" becomes "it needs Java 21, you have 17": the number on the download
    page and the number in the error differ by 44.
  * Classes under META-INF/versions/ are excluded from that maximum on purpose.
    They are the multi-release mechanism, present so a NEWER Java can pick them
    up, and counting them demands a Java the program does not require. Checked
    against a real JVM: a jar carrying a class marked for a Java that does not
    exist yet still runs, and Tandem still says 21.
  * A manifest Class-Path is checked against the folder before running. Java's
    answer when a sibling jar is missing names a class, never the absent file.
    The 72-byte line folding is undone first - a wrapped Class-Path splits file
    names in the middle, and reading it line by line yields paths that do not
    exist.
  * A machine upgraded from an older version never claimed the new formats. The
    first-run mark was an empty file, so "already run once" meant "never again",
    and the double click on a .AppImage or a .jar went on doing nothing - the
    exact bug this project exists to kill, reintroduced by the mechanism
    meant to respect the owner's choices. Reproduced by installing 3.7 over
    3.6 on a real machine: .jar still answered openjdk-21-java.desktop, and the
    self-test said so out loud.
    The mark now records which version did the work. On an upgrade the prefix
    scan is NOT repeated, and tandem-repair runs in a new --somente-novos mode
    that claims only the types this machine has never claimed - kept in
    tipos-aplicados.txt. A type the owner has never seen Tandem own carries no
    decision of his to overwrite; one he re-pointed on purpose is left alone.
  * The type-to-handler lookup in tandem-repair matched a newline-separated list
    with a pattern looking for spaces, so every type came out associated with an
    empty handler - "application/java-archive=" - which reads to the system
    as no default at all and to a person as a job done. The suite caught it
    before it was ever committed; reading the code did not. An unresolvable
    handler is now refused and logged instead of written.
  * tandem preparar installs the Java and the FUSE library too, and doctor
    reports both, along with the machine's processor and how many AppImages
    Tandem has put in the menu. The self-test exercises the two new readers
    rather than listing them, and now checks the file association of all four
    formats instead of only the .exe.
  * tandem programas lists AppImages next to the Windows programs. For the
    owner they are the same thing - something he installed with Tandem.
  * A version number read off a file becomes part of a command that runs as
    root when Tandem offers to install the Java a program asks for. It is
    reduced to digits before it gets there.
  * tandem-apk reached for /usr/lib/tandem/apkinfo.py with the path nailed
    down, so exercising it from a working copy silently read the INSTALLED
    library instead. The executables all honour TANDEM_LIB; now the sibling
    binaries honour TANDEM_BIN for the same reason, and the panel can be
    exercised without installing the package.
  * The manual pointed at docs/FORMATO-LISTA.md, renamed when the repository
    went English.
  * A CI harness runs real Windows software through Tandem weekly - PuTTY,
    Notepad++, 7-Zip and WinMerge, pinned by sha256 - and looks at the screen
    afterwards with xdotool instead of trusting an exit code. It also
    cross-checks peinfo.py against objdump on every binary it downloads. The
    project's largest uncertainty was never the mechanism, it was the sample.

 -- Paulo Eduardo <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 09 Aug 2026 03:00:00 +0000

tandem (3.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The whole repository is now written in English - comments, documentation,
    this changelog - and CLAUDE.md records that as a standing directive. Four
    deliberate exceptions, all for the same reason: the product's user is a
    Brazilian shop owner who is not a programmer. Strings shown to the user,
    the command names they type, anything shipped inside the package
    (man/tandem.1, the .desktop entries, the pt_BR MIME comments) and the
    LEIAME/CONTRIBUINDO pair stay in Portuguese. The short form: the
    repository is English, the product is Portuguese.
  * Five defects found by an adversarial audit, each one reproduced on the
    machine before being believed.
  * A multi-line value corrupted the memory file permanently. The format is
    one KEY=VALUE per line and the bitness message is five lines; the rewrite
    filter only removed the first physical line, so every run left the
    continuation lines behind as orphans and appended a fresh copy. Four runs,
    twenty-two lines, three blocks of garbage, growing forever. Values are now
    escaped on write and unescaped on read, and the rewrite drops orphan lines
    left by earlier versions.
  * The rescue copy told the truth about only two of its three outcomes.
    "There was nothing to save" and "there was data and the copy FAILED" both
    returned 1, and all three destructive paths carried on deleting either
    way - reproduced with a full disk. They are now distinct codes, and a
    failed copy stops the deletion: the double-click path refuses outright,
    the two interactive ones ask with the risk spelled out.
  * The data search lost the exit status of its own find by running it inside
    a pipe. A prefix big enough to hit the 60 s timeout looked exactly like a
    prefix with no data at all - to a caller that was about to delete
    something. The timeout now propagates as a failed copy.
  * wmvcore.dll pointed at wmp9 for every program. wmp9 has no real win64
    branch: its payload is the 32-bit XP installer, which lands in syswow64
    and is useless to a 64-bit program. wmp11 does have one, and its overrides
    are a strict superset. A 64-bit program asking for wmvcore.dll now gets
    wmp11.
  * The list of 32-bit-only verbs is now classified from the INSTALLED
    winetricks instead of being written down here. The fixed list named eight
    verbs; an inventory found 42, 38 of them reachable from a real Wine log. A
    list that only covers what somebody remembered to add covers nothing, and
    winetricks is updated from outside this project. The eight remain as the
    fallback for when winetricks cannot be read.
  * The README and LEIAME stopped pointing the main installation path at an
    empty Releases page. Until a release exists, they show the build, which
    needs neither a Debian host nor dpkg-deb.
  * The test suite is in English too, and the runner API with it: pass, fail,
    equal, skip, section. A blanket rename is exactly how a test file gets
    damaged invisibly - rewrite an EXPECTED value or a "case" pattern along
    with the prose around it and the test keeps passing while comparing the
    wrong thing. It happened during this very change: *...continua faltando*
    became *...continua missing*, and the pattern stopped matching the message
    Tandem actually produces. Both lists are now guarded by a checksum, so the
    next bulk edit cannot touch them quietly.
  * 309 tests.

 -- Paulo Eduardo <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 09 Aug 2026 02:00:00 +0000

tandem (3.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The repository is now ready for people from outside: CONTRIBUTING.md and
    CONTRIBUINDO.md carry the five rules that do not bend and the evidence
    bar; the issue templates already ask for the output of "tandem socorro"
    and the line from "tandem contribuir"; there is a PR template; and a
    release workflow builds the .deb, runs the suite and lintian, really
    installs and purges it, and only then publishes. The README had been
    pointing at Releases for thirteen versions and no release existed.
  * Real screenshots of the program's own windows in the README and LEIAME,
    and both now list all 20 commands. They described 9, and claimed Tandem
    does not install Wine or Waydroid, which "tandem preparar" has been doing
    since 2.x.
  * Everything written in the repository is now in English - comments, test
    names, documentation, this changelog. Messages to the user stay in
    Portuguese: that is rule number 2, and the target user is a Brazilian shop
    owner who is not a programmer.
  * The verb is now chosen by the program's bitness. A verb-by-verb survey of
    the installed winetricks: most modern verbs already install both payloads
    on their own, exactly ONE has a 64-bit sibling (xact -> xact_x64), and
    eight are 32-bit-only with no sibling at all. For those eight, on a 64-bit
    program, Tandem warns BEFORE installing that it probably will not help -
    instead of the owner finding out after half an hour of downloading. It
    does not block: it explains and lets them decide.
  * Delivery proof now also applies on the memory/list shortcut, which was the
    one path still writing the receipt from the winetricks exit code alone -
    bypassing the entire 3.3 thesis, and doing so exactly where the lesson
    comes from outside and deserves more suspicion, not less. The same
    shortcut gained the suspend inhibitor (it can also run dotnet48, at half
    an hour) and the verb-name validation that recipes already had and the
    list did not.
  * The list's machine count reaches the user: "on 340 machines this program
    needed these components" is the one thing the list knows that no forum
    does. It was specified, read by a function, tested, and never shown.
  * Fetching the list distinguishes "no internet" from "the list does not
    exist yet". A 404 was sending the owner to check their router because of a
    file that had not been published.
  * The documentation-drift test now EXTRACTS the commands from the main case
    statement instead of using a fixed list. With a fixed list it went green
    while four new commands were in no document at all.
  * Recipes were teaching the wrong import syntax, so whoever received one hit
    a usage error. The manual gained "version", "help", the five directories
    Tandem creates and the environment variables; and its date, frozen at
    2025-01-01 for thirteen versions, became real.
  * "curl | wget" enters Recommends: the community list depends on one of the
    two and neither was declared.
  * 294 tests.

 -- Paulo Eduardo <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0000

tandem (3.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * "tandem dados": the ENVIRONMENT rebuilds in twenty minutes, DATA never
    does. Nothing in the project separated the two, and three code paths were
    deleting the owner's data with no copy - the rm -rf of an incomplete
    prefix, restore, and the program's own uninstaller. All three now save
    first. The search does not guess: Windows user folders, plus data files
    dropped inside the program's own directory, which is where Brazilian
    commercial software keeps its database. Restoring never overwrites what is
    already there.
  * Silent success. Exit code 0 used to mean "it worked", but Wine's
    characteristic failure with commercial software is opening and being
    subtly wrong. Tandem now asks once per program, stores the answer, and the
    recipe comes out marked with where its confidence came from: "confirmado"
    by a person weighs differently from "so-abriu". Exiting in under three
    seconds is no longer celebrated.
  * Bitness. The first time the loop ran with REAL winetricks, the mfc42 verb
    exited 0, delivered the file - into syswow64, the 32-bit folder - and the
    64-bit program still could not find it. The 3.3 delivery proof looked in
    both folders, approved, and wrote the receipt: the dead end again, now
    with a receipt on top. The check became per-architecture, and there is a
    third outcome with a message of its own: it arrived, in a bitness this
    program cannot use. That is not a defect in the machine - it is a limit of
    whoever distributes the component.
  * The auditor's blind spot, closed. The generator only read w_override_dlls,
    and vcrun2003 declares mfc71, msvcp71 and msvcr71 only in title=. The
    index was blind exactly where the table was wrong. It goes from 246 to 274
    DLLs.
  * exec WITHOUT A COMMAND applies its redirections to the whole shell.
    "exec 7> file 2>/dev/null" did not silence the exec: it silenced stderr
    for all the rest of the program. With no graphical session, the loop
    detected, translated and assembled the correct message - and exited 53
    with zero bytes. Four occurrences.
  * systemd-inhibit exists and does not work without D-Bus, and it took
    winetricks down with it; the owner was told to check an internet
    connection that was perfectly fine. Presence is not function.
  * Community list, on the ad-blocker filter-list model: a static text file
    fetched over HTTPS, no server, no account, no per-user cost. Down is
    automatic; UP is not - "tandem contribuir" builds the standardised line
    and shows it in full, and the owner is the one who sends it. The record
    carries no path, username, machine name, IP or log, and the generator
    refuses to produce it if any of those appear. Format in
    docs/LIST-FORMAT.md.
  * "tandem socorro": a single file with the diagnosis, the self-test, what
    was learned and the logs, to send to someone who understands. Remote
    support stops depending on dictating commands over the phone.
  * The executables honour TANDEM_LIB, which is what made it possible to
    exercise the whole loop in a test. 271 tests.

 -- Paulo Eduardo <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0000

tandem (3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Delivery proof. winetricks exiting 0 says that IT finished, not that the
    missing file arrived - and Tandem was treating the two as the same thing.
    A wrong translation wrote a receipt exactly like a correct one, and a
    receipt is permanent: on the next attempt the program said "I already
    installed what this program was asking for" and gave up, with the real
    cause untouched. That is precisely the damage the atl*.dll entries did by
    pointing at the Adobe Type Manager. Now, after installing, Tandem checks
    whether the requested DLL appeared in the prefix. Absence of proof does
    not condemn; only a proven contradiction holds the receipt back.
  * When delivery is not confirmed, three things change at once: there is no
    receipt, the DLL/verb pair goes to traducao-suspeita.tsv, and memory does
    NOT learn the negative lesson - it would travel with the recipe to another
    machine and teach the same mistake there. The message now takes the blame
    and names the file, instead of sending the owner hunting for a defect in a
    machine that is perfectly fine.
  * The same verb is not reinstalled twice in one run after delivery fails.
    That would be thirty minutes thrown away, in the .NET case.
  * The executables now honour TANDEM_LIB when locating the libraries. With
    the path hard-coded to /usr/lib/tandem there was no way to exercise the
    run->detect->install loop without installing the package - and that loop
    was precisely the thing that had never run, in the field or in a test.
  * Twelve new tests run the whole of tandem-exe against a fake wine and a
    fake winetricks, covering both outcomes and the second run. 218 tests in
    total.

 -- Paulo Eduardo <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

tandem (3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: "tandem autoteste". doctor LISTS what exists; the self-test
    EXERCISES and says what works - and the difference has already been
    expensive here. Five defects found in the field were invisible to a list:
    zenity installed but refusing accented text, the progress pipe killing the
    process when written to, the lock that could not be created, the diagnosis
    writing zero bytes to a file, and the error "shown" in a window that never
    opened. Where it cannot exercise, it says it skipped instead of pretending
    it approved.
  * The repository gains an evidence gate (proofgate.json) and CI. The gate
    could not see the suite: this is a shell project with its own runner, and
    automatic detection only knows ecosystems with a manifest - it went green
    without running a single test. It now runs the 206 tests, shellcheck and
    the syntax check, and declares the files that only make sense together
    (control with changelog, tandem with the manual, winedeps with the tests).
  * The project's first CI: suite, packaging, lintian with no warnings,
    reproducible build, and a real install-configure-purge cycle on Ubuntu
    24.04, which is the base of Zorin 18.
  * The manual documents the new commands, and a test checks both directions:
    no command is left undocumented, and the manual promises no command that
    does not exist.

